Subject: [PATCH] mempool(v2): reconcile overlay algorithms and native
 transaction bookkeeping

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
No source semantics are added or removed by this history operation.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Add libFuzzer harnesses covering V2 v7 wire codecs, Lotus V2 VM execution,
Merklix set reconciliation, and UTXO shard fast sync.

Original-Commit: aa56a04645b27e97d6d55b9292e73c5cb6065cdf
Original-Patch: v2/024
Split-Concern: overlay

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Retain the original native UTXO overlay algorithms and native state/monetary snapshot anchoring. Keep the already-working known-parent iterator API and actual bulk-clear implementation rather than reversing them temporarily before later native batch-resolution consumers restore them. Retain token-input filtering and snapshot lifecycle hooks; omit duplicate ConnectBlockReset placement.

(cherry picked from commit 9f9be08e348b77a22bfc6e1921b8a275d643ad7a)

